{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries","id":1376396,"title":"Help with Mysteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-24T06:22:48-07:00","id":1376396,"title":"Help with Mysteries","content":"Hello,<br /> so yeah,I have trouble coming up with Mysteries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, so what are some interesting Mysteries that you have come up with or used?<br /> Because I'm currently blanking.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes I know mysteries for Mage threads are basically a dime a dozen out there, BUT they are rather useless to me (and I guess a lot of other people).<br /> <br /> Why? They are just very basic plot hooks, a la here is something strange and interesting happening... and I can come up whit dozens of strange and interesting things happening.<br /> <br /> My issue lies with coming up whit what interesting thing actually causes those happenings and strange occurrences. That's what I'm currently blanking on.^^ (and I bet a lot of other people have trouble wit who ask fro help with Mysteries).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T09:08:52-07:00","id":1376403,"title":"","content":"Typically what I do is to think about the setting and how it has rules. Then I pick a rule and break it.<br /> <br /> Hallows only go up to 5 dots. So what if I make Vesuvius into a 6+ dot Hallow? It never runs out. I don\u2019t want that to be exploited too heavily, so I make the mana from it somewhat volatile. How do I do that? Vesuvius in Mage Sight never stopped erupting, the mana is molten lava. Being exposed to it automatically forces the activation of Mage Sight, and like with Apocalypse you run the risk of burning out your eyes. So it\u2019s really dangerous to hang out on Vesuvius, why do Mages go there? Hmm, well, there are places on Vesuvius where you can leave things to soak in this volatile mana and they will become Perfected in just a few days regardless of Size and without needing to be rested.<br /> <br /> Another example. Everything that dies is eventually swept into the Underworld. I want a heavily haunted place though. So in this one place there are no Avernian Gates. In Twilight there\u2019s a wall that acts as a dam keeping everything in. Nothing that has ever died or been destroyed in this place ever goes away from Twilight because without the Gates there\u2019s nowhere for it to go. For fun I\u2019ll just also mention that ghosts in this place don\u2019t suffer Essence bleed from existing. Why do Mages go here? To investigate the wall, and the phenomenon as a whole. To move ghosts of things they wish to preserve there. Other reasons I may not have thought of yet.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really worry about why it\u2019s happening. Most Mages will be more interested in using the Mystery for some reason than they will in explaining why it\u2019s happening. If I must though I\u2019ll tie it to the setting\u2019s mythology. Vesuvius was a centaur that angered Zeus, so there\u2019s a Bound in the center of the Volcano or something. Or for the ghost one, a huge number of ghosts were created by a battle or something similarly devastating and they got to work bricking up the Avernian Gates and built the wall. Now they\u2019re stuck, and more ghost stuff keeps moving in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T09:52:28-07:00","id":1376571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376403#post1376403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really worry about why it\u2019s happening.</div> </div> </div> </div> But don't you need at least a good idea of why, to know what information your players get under Mage Sight?<br /> But I guess the Mysteries you describe are more \u201csetting Mysteries\u201d, something that informs the background of your setting/campaign, not the immediate task/quest/problem players want to deal with.<br /> I'm thinking more of mysteries that present the \u201cquest\u201d so to say.<br /> Something like: \u201cChildren are vanishing. At first, their guardians claim that they've gone to camp for the week. Soon, they forget they had kids at all. And that's when the post cards begging for help (and which Sleepers cannot see) start coming in...\u201d<br /> So players want to find out whats up with that.<br /> Now in a mortal game I can keep things vague and mysterious(or a Vampire,Werewolf etc. hell, even a MtAc game). In a mage game, I need to know what does Mage Sight revel, in mechanical terms, when they look at the post card's or the guardians. Which again should ideally be somehow connected to what lies further down the line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T18:34:50-07:00","id":1376638,"title":"","content":"Focused Mage Sight lets the mage peer into the Supernal to understand the Mystery. They literally hallucinate the right answer, even when they otherwise had no business knowing it. But those answers are presented steeped in the symbolism of their Path and Legacy. The more they look past its Opacity, the more the vision reveals. <br /> <br /> The difficulty lies in interpretating it. That is when Knowing and Unveiling spells aid them, they are precision tools. The Focused Sight is a top down look at the system. The Knowing and Unveiling practices are bottom up tools that let you open the black boxes and understand individual parts. Combining both lets them build a hollistic view of the Mystery.<br /> <br /> I believe Signs of Sorcery also has more in-depth information on building Mysteries. I also posted a recent example of them in use, perhaps it can be of aid:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1372262-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-solving-a-mystery-and-using-magic\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nd-using-magic</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-25-2020, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T02:00:57-07:00","id":1376688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376571#post1376571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't you need at least a good idea of why, to know what information your players get under Mage Sight?<br /> But I guess the Mysteries you describe are more \u201csetting Mysteries\u201d, something that informs the background of your setting/campaign, not the immediate task/quest/problem players want to deal with.<br /> I'm thinking more of mysteries that present the \u201cquest\u201d so to say.<br /> Something like: \u201cChildren are vanishing. At first, their guardians claim that they've gone to camp for the week. Soon, they forget they had kids at all. And that's when the post cards begging for help (and which Sleepers cannot see) start coming in...\u201d<br /> So players want to find out whats up with that.<br /> Now in a mortal game I can keep things vague and mysterious(or a Vampire,Werewolf etc. hell, even a MtAc game). In a mage game, I need to know what does Mage Sight revel, in mechanical terms, when they look at the post card's or the guardians. Which again should ideally be somehow connected to what lies further down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's pretty easy. Build your &quot;quests&quot; around your Setting Mystery. That's what it's there for. An unexpected explosion of Vesuvian Mana occurs where a bunch of inexperienced Mages are gathered. Why?<br /> <br /> A particularly potent ghost has become trapped inside the wall somehow, and is causing trouble. If ghosts require going to the Underworld to get above Rank 2, then how did this Rank 4 monstrosity get here?<br /> <br /> The Runewalks of London can boost a spell or alter a Mage's experiences in countless ways that lead to weirdness.<br /> <br /> The future ghosts of Tucson drop hints as to what's coming, and some Mage exploits that to set up a scenario that accomplishes some occult rite that pollutes the area with their influence.<br /> <br /> A Sleepwalker gets fed up with his minder and lures them into a trap in an Ansho, and then somehow makes the Ansho move to hide the circumstances around the Mage's death. Can they figure it out?<br /> <br /> An artifact is left behind by one of the portals from Salamanca, now the Mage's are trying to figure out how it works, and what it is because it doesn't seem to respond to magic. The portal it came from quickly closed behind it, so determining its point of origin is also proving problematic.<br /> <br /> The Setting is there to be used. The Mages who are in the Setting use the Mystery to do...whatever it is they're doing. That's why they're there in the first place. If the Setting Mystery wasn't relevant to their interests then they're just passing through or they're probably aren't there at all. This is true for PCs and NPCs and having a handle on that is going to make it a lot easier for you to determine why things happen in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T04:58:22-07:00","id":1376697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376638#post1376638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focused Mage Sight lets the mage peer into the Supernal to understand the Mystery. They literally hallucinate the right answer, even when they otherwise had no business knowing it. But those answers are presented steeped in the symbolism of their Path and Legacy. The more they look past its Opacity, the more the vision reveals.<br /> <br /> The difficulty lies in interpretating it. That is when Knowing and Unveiling spells aid them, they are precision tools. The Focused Sight is a top down look at the system. The Knowing and Unveiling practices are bottom up tools that let you open the black boxes and understand individual parts. Combining both lets them build a hollistic view of the Mystery.<br /> <br /> I believe Signs of Sorcery also has more in-depth information on building Mysteries. I also posted a recent example of them in use, perhaps it can be of aid:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1372262-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-solving-a-mystery-and-using-magic\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nd-using-magic</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Ok.<br /> So as I understand it basic Focused Mage Sight gives you those vague, impressionist, narrative clues.<br /> But than Scrutiny and Revelation gives the character such a deep and precise understanding of the Mystery that it translates to the player gaining clear mechanical information about the Mystery.<br /> Was I wrong there? ( I also thought about not using the rules for Scrutiny, since as I read it it seem like just an endless array of dice rolls without much Narrative impact and than an infodump)<br /> <br /> Also no unfortunately Signs of Sorcery doesn't contain anything on building Mysteries, which was my biggest letdown with the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T05:13:04-07:00","id":1376698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376688#post1376688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's pretty easy. Build your &quot;quests&quot; around your Setting Mystery. That's what it's there for. An unexpected explosion of Vesuvian Mana occurs where a bunch of inexperienced Mages are gathered. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div> So in other word just use Mysteries wit an Opacity so high that there is no chance in hell they will ever whittle it down to 0?<br /> Which I don't know than I'd rather not use the Scrutiny+Revelation rules at all.<br /> On the other hand I might have gotten things wrong all along as to how much mechanical information Mage Sight reveals....^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T09:19:21-07:00","id":1376720,"title":"","content":"If your looking for more 'episodic' Mysteries that don't interact with your setting Mystery, might I suggest flipping your thinking slightly? Rather than starting with the Mystery mechanics, instead look at the huge range of setting elements available and pick a few for your latest story arc to center around. The Mysteries then flow naturally from there as the players start to investigate. The whole deal with Opacity and so on are just one way for them to deduce the answers they want. Mrmdubois point about how Mysteries are often things that break the established rules is also really important.<br /> <br /> For example say you decide a Rapt with an Obsession with the Astral is lurking in your cabals territory. The PC's might come across a neighbour who has been tormented by a loose Geotia. Opacity 3 mystery to work out the nature of the attacker. The Rapt uses unknown magic to rip open Iris's to the Temenos and lures Sleepers into them. The Iris is an Opacity 5 mystery to get an idea about what it is, where it goes and how to open it. Hooded strangers start following people in the neighbourhood, threatening violence if they don't tell the stranger all about what they dreamed last night. Opacity 5 to determine its the Rapts Tulpa.<br /> <br /> The Focused Mage sight rules are just one tool for your players to use to understand (and a convienient way for you to drop clue's about) whatever odd thing you have dreamed up for them to poke at today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T11:33:44-07:00","id":1376733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376698#post1376698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So in other word just use Mysteries wit an Opacity so high that there is no chance in hell they will ever whittle it down to 0?<br /> Which I don't know than I'd rather not use the Scrutiny+Revelation rules at all.<br /> On the other hand I might have gotten things wrong all along as to how much mechanical information Mage Sight reveals....^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Opacity for Setting Mysteries isn't supposed to be so high that it can't be cracked. Many are only Opacity 5. Just because you reveal the narrative information of, &quot;What is this?&quot; though doesn't mean you know what all you can do with it. One of the reason Setting Mysteries remain mysterious is not because no one knows what they do, but no one knows all the possible things they can do, and the only way to find out is to experiment. London is an obvious example. Rune Walks can do pretty much anything, there's no way to know what it will do until you go on one.<br /> <br /> When you're doing more episodic Mysteries you may find it helpful to use these derivatives of what a Setting Mystery might be made to do (or do on it's own) to create smaller Mysteries. The source will be fairly obvious to the ST, because they will know that something weird has happened to the Setting, which means someone or something must have happened to it. If you figure that in London some children start to disappear and only the Mages and Sleepwalkers can remember them or read the ransom notes on the postcards, then you can also safely figure that it probably involved a Rune Walk somehow. Which means a Mage probably did it. From there you can look at your cast of NPCs and figure out which one might have the motive based on their Obsessions, or maybe they did it by accident, or maybe you have to make a new NPC entirely who is trying to use the Rune Walks to steal children for some nefarious purpose.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you decide that something momentous is going to happen in London, you want to signal that somehow, so you start making all the Rune Walks no matter how they're navigated or begun end up at the same place with portents of doom clinging to there usual effects.<br /> <br /> So you see here you can attack it from either end, either coming up with the Mystery beforehand, and then working backward to the cause and making it a bit easier for yourself by remembering the weirdness you've already decided you want in your setting. Or you can figure out what weird thing you want to have happen and then move forward to what kind of things that does to the Setting. Either way, it ends up answering the why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T18:20:51-07:00","id":1376757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376396-help-with-mysteries?p=1376697#post1376697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ok.<br /> So as I understand it basic Focused Mage Sight gives you those vague, impressionist, narrative clues.<br /> But than Scrutiny and Revelation gives the character such a deep and precise understanding of the Mystery that it translates to the player gaining clear mechanical information about the Mystery.<br /> Was I wrong there? ( I also thought about not using the rules for Scrutiny, since as I read it it seem like just an endless array of dice rolls without much Narrative impact and than an infodump)<br /> <br /> Also no unfortunately Signs of Sorcery doesn't contain anything on building Mysteries, which was my biggest letdown with the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, normal focused sight gives the surface information. But Revelation and Scrutiny are all about uncovering more details. So you can give more precise info as they lower Opacity. That is fine, especially since a stronger cabal will blast through low Opacity. Especially if they have a powerful Prime practitioner.<br /> <br /> Remember that mages are the best equipped splat for investigation. Don't rely on keeping things hidden from them, but rather on what dilemmas that knowledge brings. Remember that indirection (multiple layers of favor trading and proxies) and misdirection (focusing the attention of the mage away from the topic rather than trying to hide it) are a lot more powerful, since they take a lot more time and attention to untangle without leaving loose ends.<br /> <br /> Lastly, this article had some interesting ideas on it, perhaps it can be useful:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/07/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-focused-mage.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/07/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-focused-mage.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/07/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-focused-mage.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/07/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-focused-mage.html?m=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}